7:[["$","$Lf",null,{}],["$","div",null,{"ref":"$undefined","className":"sm:px-8 mt-16 sm:mt-32","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl lg:px-8","children":["$","div",null,{"ref":"$undefined","className":"relative px-4 sm:px-8 lg:px-12","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-2xl lg:max-w-5xl","children":[["$","$L5",null,{"href":"/en/articles","className":"text-sm font-medium text-orange-500 transition hover:text-orange-600 dark:hover:text-orange-400","children":"Back to articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-10 grid gap-16 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_18rem]","children":[["$","article",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.32em] text-orange-500","children":"Fundamentals"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 sm:text-5xl dark:text-zinc-100","children":"Object-Oriented Programming Basics"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-6 max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400","children":"A practical introduction to OOP: classes, objects, encapsulation, abstraction, inheritance, and polymorphism with code examples."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative mt-10 aspect-[16/9] overflow-hidden rounded-3xl bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/oop-basics.svg","alt":"Object-Oriented Programming Basics","className":"h-full w-full object-cover"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-12 space-y-12","children":[["$","section","Background",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":"Background"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400","children":[[["$","p","Object-oriented programming models software around real-world entities. Instead of thinking only in functions, we model state and behavior together in objects.",{"children":"Object-oriented programming models software around real-world entities. Instead of thinking only in functions, we model state and behavior together in objects."}],["$","p","A class acts as a blueprint, and an object is an instance created from that blueprint. Attributes represent state, while methods represent behavior.",{"children":"A class acts as a blueprint, and an object is an instance created from that blueprint. Attributes represent state, while methods represent behavior."}]],"$undefined"]}]]}],["$","section","OOP building blocks",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":"OOP building blocks"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400","children":[[["$","p","Objects: real entities with state and behavior. A calculator can be on or off (state) and can add or multiply (behavior).",{"children":"Objects: real entities with state and behavior. A calculator can be on or off (state) and can add or multiply (behavior)."}],["$","p","Classes: templates for creating objects with shared structure and behavior.",{"children":"Classes: templates for creating objects with shared structure and behavior."}],["$","p","Attributes: variables that hold object state.",{"children":"Attributes: variables that hold object state."}],["$","p","Methods: functions attached to classes that define behavior.",{"children":"Methods: functions attached to classes that define behavior."}]],"$undefined"]}]]}],["$","section","1) Encapsulation and data hiding",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":"1) Encapsulation and data hiding"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400","children":[[["$","p","Encapsulation hides internal data and exposes safe public methods. A common convention is keeping class variables private and interacting through getters/setters or domain methods.",{"children":"Encapsulation hides internal data and exposes safe public methods. A common convention is keeping class variables private and interacting through getters/setters or domain methods."}],["$","p","This improves maintainability, control over read/write access, and protects internal consistency.",{"children":"This improves maintainability, control over read/write access, and protects internal consistency."}]],[["$","pre","1) Encapsulation and data hiding-code-0",{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-800 dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":["$","code",null,{"className":"language-python","children":"class BankAccount:\n    def __init__(self, owner, balance=0):\n        self.owner = owner\n        self.__balance = balance  # private by convention\n\n    def deposit(self, amount):\n        if amount > 0:\n            self.__balance += amount\n\n    def withdraw(self, amount):\n        if 0 < amount <= self.__balance:\n            self.__balance -= amount\n            return True\n        return False\n\n    def get_balance(self):\n        return self.__balance"}]}]]]}]]}],["$","section","2) Abstraction",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":"2) Abstraction"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400","children":[[["$","p","Abstraction exposes only what users need and hides implementation details. It reduces cognitive load and keeps interfaces focused.",{"children":"Abstraction exposes only what users need and hides implementation details. It reduces cognitive load and keeps interfaces focused."}],["$","p","In practice, we define a clear contract and allow concrete classes to implement details behind that contract.",{"children":"In practice, we define a clear contract and allow concrete classes to implement details behind that contract."}]],[["$","pre","2) Abstraction-code-0",{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-800 dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":["$","code",null,{"className":"language-python","children":"from abc import ABC, abstractmethod\n\nclass PaymentProcessor(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    def pay(self, amount):\n        pass\n\nclass StripeProcessor(PaymentProcessor):\n    def pay(self, amount):\n        return f\"Paid ${amount} with Stripe\"\n\nclass PaypalProcessor(PaymentProcessor):\n    def pay(self, amount):\n        return f\"Paid ${amount} with PayPal\""}]}]]]}]]}],["$","section","3) Inheritance, generalization, and specialization",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":"3) Inheritance, generalization, and specialization"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400","children":[[["$","p","Inheritance models IS-A relationships. A child class reuses and extends parent behavior.",{"children":"Inheritance models IS-A relationships. A child class reuses and extends parent behavior."}],["$","p","Generalization extracts shared behavior into a parent class, while specialization defines child classes with specific behavior.",{"children":"Generalization extracts shared behavior into a parent class, while specialization defines child classes with specific behavior."}],["$","p","This supports reuse, extensibility, and better organization when multiple classes share common logic.",{"children":"This supports reuse, extensibility, and better organization when multiple classes share common logic."}]],[["$","pre","3) Inheritance, generalization, and specialization-code-0",{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-800 dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":["$","code",null,{"className":"language-python","children":"class Shape:\n    def area(self):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\nclass Rectangle(Shape):\n    def __init__(self, w, h):\n        self.w = w\n        self.h = h\n\n    def area(self):\n        return self.w * self.h\n\nclass Square(Rectangle):\n    def __init__(self, side):\n        super().__init__(side, side)"}]}]]]}]]}],["$","section","4) Polymorphism",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":"4) Polymorphism"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400","children":[[["$","p","Polymorphism means one interface, many implementations. You can treat different subclasses through the same parent contract.",{"children":"Polymorphism means one interface, many implementations. You can treat different subclasses through the same parent contract."}],["$","p","Dynamic polymorphism is usually method overriding at runtime. Static polymorphism is typically method overloading/operator overloading depending on language support.",{"children":"Dynamic polymorphism is usually method overriding at runtime. Static polymorphism is typically method overloading/operator overloading depending on language support."}]],[["$","pre","4) Polymorphism-code-0",{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-800 dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":["$","code",null,{"className":"language-python","children":"class Animal:\n    def speak(self):\n        return \"...\"\n\nclass Dog(Animal):\n    def speak(self):\n        return \"Woof\"\n\nclass Cat(Animal):\n    def speak(self):\n        return \"Meow\"\n\ndef make_it_speak(animal: Animal):\n    return animal.speak()\n\nprint(make_it_speak(Dog()))\nprint(make_it_speak(Cat()))"}]}]]]}]]}],["$","section","Inheritance modes and design caution",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":"Inheritance modes and design caution"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400","children":[[["$","p","You will hear about single, multiple, multi-level, hierarchical, and hybrid inheritance. Not every language supports each mode the same way.",{"children":"You will hear about single, multiple, multi-level, hierarchical, and hybrid inheritance. Not every language supports each mode the same way."}],["$","p","Use inheritance intentionally. If there is no clear IS-A relationship, composition is often a cleaner and safer design choice.",{"children":"Use inheritance intentionally. If there is no clear IS-A relationship, composition is often a cleaner and safer design choice."}]],"$undefined"]}]]}],["$","section","Generalization, OCP, and maintainability",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100","children":"Generalization, OCP, and maintainability"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400","children":[[["$","p","Generalization helps the open/closed principle: classes stay closed for modification but open for extension through new subclasses.",{"children":"Generalization helps the open/closed principle: classes stay closed for modification but open for extension through new subclasses."}],["$","p","When done well, OOP gives reusable modules, cleaner change boundaries, and easier long-term maintenance.",{"children":"When done well, OOP gives reusable modules, cleaner change boundaries, and easier long-term maintenance."}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-zinc-200/70 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm shadow-zinc-900/5 dark:border-zinc-700/60 dark:bg-zinc-900/80 dark:shadow-black/20","children":["$","dl",null,{"className":"space-y-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400","children":"Published"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300","children":"April 19, 2026"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400","children":"Updated"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300","children":"April 19, 2026"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400","children":"Category"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300","children":"Fundamentals"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400","children":"Topics"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2","children":[["$","span","OOP",{"className":"rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-300","children":"OOP"}],["$","span","Programming Basics",{"className":"rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-300","children":"Programming Basics"}],["$","span","Design",{"className":"rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-3 py-1 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-300","children":"Design"}]]}]]}]]}]}]}]]}]]}]}]}]}]]
